    {
      "id": "claim_3270e7ddb3a848c79196bc8659ba7301",
      "statement": "The verdict surface is minimal: VerificationResult.status is typed 'RESOLVED' | 'UNRESOLVED' | 'UNKNOWN'; shipped paths emit RESOLVED when the target is derived and UNKNOWN with an evidence note when it is not, with UNRESOLVED reserved by the type but not produced by v1 code; an UNKNOWN verdict is a legitimate auditable 'cannot yet be proven' outcome, not a hard fail, so downstream consumers can distinguish 'proven wrong' from 'cannot yet be proven' [v1].",
